# `declaration:rows`' red half (tflw `G10`, `D1384`). `rows-counted.tflw`'s three rows under a block
# whose first line claims two 200s. It is a `check`, so it fails and the block goes on: the second
# line runs and passes, and the third, an `expect` that is also wrong, fails and ends the block before
# the fourth, which is never run. Every row still passes on its own.

with each
  | ms     |
  | 0      |
  | 600000 |
  | 600000 |
test "row {ms} asks once"
  api GET /after/{ms}
  expect status is less than 600
rows
  check exactly 2 rows status equals 200
  expect 2 rows status equals 503
  expect every row status equals 200
  expect no rows status equals 500
